## Context

Optional follow-up to measured ranking failures, not a mandatory corpus-wide backfill. Missing subjective dimensions must not prevent baseline ranking.

Design baseline: v7. v6 was merged by PR #903 and is frozen at `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-v6.md`; v7 closes the acceptance review's four §12.1 conditions and settles the nomenclature, leaving the architecture and this ticket's scope unchanged. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`, `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-nomenclature.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Library ranking inputs; evaluation findings from 0918; representative existing bodies; model/provenance conventions.

## Actions

1. Only proceed if evaluation identifies a failure plausibly improved by a declared annotation.
2. Define a small vocabulary and annotated comparison sample; record disagreements as evidence, not proof the vocabulary alone is wrong.
3. Compare gains before proposing corpus-wide annotation. Preserve explicit defaults for unannotated bodies and record model/source provenance.
4. No mandatory guard category, occurrence-based authority or silent budget increase.

## Test

Unannotated body remains rankable under baseline defaults. Compare fixed-policy selections and task outcomes with/without sample annotations, preserving evidence and scope.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v7, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Sample result and cost justify any expansion, or the proposal remains deferred.
- [ ] No reject-all-unannotated test or automatic full-corpus model pass.
- [ ] Not a prerequisite for core completion.
